NEARS-1933 QA — live repro, 2026-08-21, emulator-5570

$ bash scripts/qa-tools/qa_stall_backend.sh start --port 8091
[qa_stall_backend] started pid=17652 port=8091 log=/tmp/qa_stall_backend_8091.log
port=8091 pid=17652

$ bash scripts/qa-tools/qa_stall_backend.sh status
port 8091: pid=17652 running (ps state=S)
$ echo exit=$?
exit=1                      <-- BUG: instance listed successfully, should be exit 0

$ bash scripts/qa-tools/qa_stall_backend.sh stop --port 8091
[qa_stall_backend] stopped and confirmed gone: pid=17652 port=8091

$ bash scripts/qa-tools/qa_stall_backend.sh status
no qa_stall_backend instances recorded
$ echo exit=$?
exit=0                      <-- correct (no-instance case)

Root cause (read in scripts/qa-tools/qa_stall_backend.sh cmd_status(), no-arg branch):
  [[ "$any" -eq 0 ]] && echo "no qa_stall_backend instances recorded"
This is the LAST statement in the function. When any=1 (an instance WAS found
and printed), the `[[ ]]` test is false, so the `&&` short-circuits and the
compound statement's exit status is 1 (the test's own falsy result) -- even
though the function did exactly what it was supposed to do. set -euo pipefail
does not trip here because it's the final statement of the script's dispatch
case, so the FALSE exit code becomes the script's own exit code.

Confirmed as previously flagged by the engineer during fix cycle 2 (self-check
note in the FIX-CYCLE PACKET). Does not affect AC1 or AC2 and does not block
this ticket's PASS -- flagged per the engineer's request for routing to a
follow-up/regression ticket.
